    description: "ADR-0057 rulings 1 and 4: after the merge pass, a record's attribute is a SET\nof (value, provenance) pairs — agreement is one value with two provenances,\ndisagreement is two values each with one, disjoint coverage is one value with\none provenance and no entry from the other producer. Consumers keep reading\nthe scalar slot; the scalar is produced by a per-record ARBITRATION PROPERTY,\na pure function over the preserved candidates (O(candidates), no whole-table\naccess), with ONE stamped default so ranking (ranking.py:925, :1044), slicing\n(slice.py:828, :838) and serialization all see the same value. Alternative\npolicies are opt-in reads of the candidate set, never a second default.\n\nWHY A SCHEMA CHANGE: `origin` (INV-jidat) is record-level; `confidence_source`\n(ADR-0039 ruling 2, value `composite`) is the one existing per-attribute\nprovenance and is the precedent. `meta` is not a registry (parent_type is\nwritten by 4 analyzers, read by a linker, declared nowhere), so provenance\ncannot live there. This needs a registered, schema-versioned slot on Symbol\nand Edge — patch bump of SCHEMA_VERSION, docs/schema.json and\ndocs/concept-axes.md regenerated, ir.py fields carry `# axis:` comments\n(check-multi-value-field-axis-declaration gate).\n\nPROPOSED SHAPE (the implementing PR may refine; the ADR pins the semantics,\nnot the spelling): `attribution: {field: [pass_id, ...]}` on a merged record,\nplus `alternatives: {field: [{value, origin: [pass_id]}]}` present only for\ncontested fields. Absence of both = single producer, today's records\nunchanged. Edge `evidence_type` is a candidate set too (an edge seen by two\ninference pathways is precisely ADR-0028's composite case).\n\nLAZY-FIELD CONTRACT: `edge_key` is the codebase's existing memoised field\n(ir.py:994 create, :1256 recompute-when-None, :2021 recompute-on-rewire) and\nits cost is the invalidation rule. The arbitration property must be pure over\nthe candidate set so it needs NO invalidation.\n\nACCEPTANCE: on the aardvark-dns two-arm artifact every merged node serialises\none scalar per field plus attribution; the 52 free functions show kind\nalternatives from both producers until the SCIP kind fix lands; the ADR-0043\n§8 round-trip test passes; tree-sitter-only artifacts unchanged."  # 83a7
    fields: {}  # 83a7
